Mesa's options from the program (testing.md 18.955, 20 November 2026)

Mesa reads its options - INTEL_DEBUG, LP_NUM_THREADS and the rest - from
the environment, and a Kosmos process has none (getenv answers nothing,
user/init/misc_user.c). So a program that wants to tell Mesa something
defines kosmos_mesa_option(name), answering a name with its value or
NULL, and os_get_option asks it after getenv. Weak, so a program that
defines none gives Mesa no options, as before. Found it wanted the day
anv hung the M700's render engine on the 3D Kit's first submission and
INTEL_DEBUG=bat was the way to read the batch.

--- a/src/util/os_misc.c
+++ b/src/util/os_misc.c
@@ -38,6 +38,12 @@
 
 #include <stdarg.h>
 
+#if DETECT_OS_KOSMOS
+/* Mesa's options, from the program that links it (patch 0008). Weak: a
+ * program that defines none gives Mesa none. */
+extern const char *kosmos_mesa_option(const char *name) __attribute__((weak));
+#endif
+
 
 #if DETECT_OS_WINDOWS
 
@@ -244,6 +250,14 @@
       opt = os_get_android_option(name);
    }
 #endif
+#if DETECT_OS_KOSMOS
+   /* Kosmos has no environment: a program that wants Mesa told something
+    * - INTEL_DEBUG, LP_NUM_THREADS - answers here, and one that does not
+    * leaves every option unset. */
+   if (!opt && kosmos_mesa_option != NULL) {
+      opt = kosmos_mesa_option(name);
+   }
+#endif
    return opt;
 }
 
